%% Inspectra - State Machine Diagram: 5-Tuple Connection Flow Lifecycle
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NEW : First Packet Observed (5-Tuple Registered)
    
    NEW --> ESTABLISHED : TCP 3-Way Handshake Complete\n(SYN -> SYN-ACK -> ACK)
    NEW --> CLASSIFIED : Immediate L7 Data Observed (UDP / Pre-handshake)
    NEW --> BLOCKED : Source IP / Port on Blacklist
    NEW --> CLOSED : RST Received

    ESTABLISHED --> CLASSIFIED : Payload Dissected\n(TLS SNI / HTTP Host / DNS Extracted)
    ESTABLISHED --> BLOCKED : Policy Deny Triggered\n(IP / Port Match)
    ESTABLISHED --> CLOSED : RST Received / FIN Handshake Initiated

    CLASSIFIED --> BLOCKED : Classified App / Domain on Blacklist\n(e.g., YouTube, *.tiktok.com)
    CLASSIFIED --> CLOSED : Normal Teardown (FIN + ACK) OR TCP RST
    
    BLOCKED --> BLOCKED : Future Packets Dropped (Action: DROP)
    BLOCKED --> CLOSED : TCP RST / Connection Teardown

    CLOSED --> [*] : Connection Evicted\n(cleanupStale Timeout > 300s OR LRU Eviction)
